-## Subtopics
-
-### Local Light Fields
-A variant for sparse inputs where the scene is divided into local regions, each with its own embedding network. It is chosen when the global embedding network fails to interpolate well due to large depth and texture changes. It requires more network evaluations per ray but handles sparser data better. [Link](13622-local-light-fields.md) (Note: Link placeholder as specific article not provided in sibling list, but concept is described).
-
-### Ray-Space Embedding Network
-The core component that maps 4D ray-space to an interpolable latent space. It is chosen for its ability to register rays observing the same 3D points and interpolate unobserved rays, leading to better memorization and view synthesis. [Link](13622-ray-space-embedding-network.md) (Note: Link placeholder).
